## Report

**Task:** fix `COUNT(DISTINCTCASE WHEN ...` — invalid SQL when a `Count` annotation combines a `Case` condition with `distinct=True` (per TASK.md).

**Cause** — `django/db/models/aggregates.py`:
- Template (line 17): `'%(function)s(%(distinct)s%(expressions)s)'`
- `Aggregate.as_sql` (line 71) set `extra_context['distinct'] = 'DISTINCT'` with **no trailing space**. When the expression is a `Case` (compiled to `CASE WHEN ...`), the pieces concatenate into `COUNT(DISTINCTCASE WHEN ...` — two SQL keywords fused into one identifier → syntax error. A plain distinct column (`COUNT(DISTINCT"col"`) only worked by luck, since the quote acts as a lexer delimiter.

**Fix** (one line, line 71):
```python
extra_context['distinct'] = 'DISTINCT ' if self.distinct else ''
```

**Evidence (proven):**
- Repro before fix: `COUNT(DISTINCTCASE WHEN "auth_user"."id" > %s THEN %s ELSE NULL END)`; after fix: `COUNT(DISTINCT CASE WHEN ...)` — and plain `COUNT(DISTINCT "auth_user"."id")` unchanged (FINDING-706edc).
- Django test suites `aggregation`, `aggregation_regress`, `annotations`, `expressions_case`: **251 tests, OK (7 skipped)** (FINDING-71bc5c). Note: the project's pytest command couldn't run — pytest isn't installed in the venv — so I used Django's own `tests/runtests.py` with `PYTHONPATH` pointing at this checkout (the venv's `import django` resolves here). `sqlparse` was missing from the venv; installed from a local wheel in `/tmp` (no network).
- Working tree: exactly one modified tracked file, `django/db/models/aggregates.py`; no tests added/modified, nothing committed, scratch repro removed (FINDING-8ecf70).
